    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d868">

                <pb facs="1368" n="1354" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1354"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 E.W./8–2244: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-08-28T17:00:00-04:00">August 28, 1944—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6891. For Pell. Your 6429, August 10, 6627, August 17, and 6804, August
                        22.<anchor n="86" xml:id="d868-f1"/> You may inform Hurst that this
                    Government raises no objection to the statement enclosed in your despatch 17295
                    of August 5, it being understood that the statement is to be given to the press
                    not for publication but in strictest confidence solely as a guide for newspapers
                    themselves in order that they may understand lines on which Commission proceeds,
                    and not as a direct communiqué from the Commission.<anchor n="87"
                        xml:id="d868-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d868-f1" n="86" xml:id="d868-f1-content">
                <p>Telegrams 6627 and 6804 not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d868-f2" n="87" xml:id="d868-f2-content">
                <p>Sir Cecil Hurst held the press conference at the Law Courts on August 30,
                    1944.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
